  ],
  "equipment_type": "Constant volume terminal unit controller",
  "applies_to": "Constant volume terminal boxes with an airflow sensor and a hot water reheat valve on the Siemens BACnet PTEC constant volume controller 550-498PA.",
  "summary": "Application 6663 runs a constant volume terminal box with hot water reheat on a Siemens BACnet PTEC controller over BACnet MS/TP. The flow loop holds OCC FLOW when occupied and the lower UNOCC FLOW when unoccupied, and the temperature loop modulates the reheat valve in both heating and cooling modes. There is no automatic heat/cool switchover; PPCL or the field panel commands HEAT.COOL to pick the seasonal setpoints.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Newer than revision Bx40",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "AI and BI objects are read-only. AO and BO objects are BACnet output objects with a priority array; the guide has no access column, so access is inferred from object type. Many AOs are calculated status values, not commands.",
    "Instances shown in braces in the guide may be unbundled at a field panel; that marking is not reproduced here.",
    "Units are given in US units (°F, cfm, ft², ft³); the guide also lists SI factory defaults.",
    "The guide covers controllers with firmware newer than revision Bx40; older firmware has separate documentation.",
    "The point database names the occupancy points OCC.UNOCC, OCC/UOC CLG/HTG STPT and UNOCC OVRD; parts of the guide text still call them DAY.NGT, DAY/NGT setpoints and NGT OVRD.",
    "FAIL MODE (BO 40) sets whether the damper opens or closes if the air velocity sensor fails; the guide text calls CLOSED the default, but the point table lists OPEN."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet PTEC Controller Constant Volume with Hot Water Reheat, Application 6663, Application Note",
    "doc_number": "140-1109",
    "revision_date": "2014-10-27",
    "url": "https://sid.siemens.com/api/khub/documents/Q2mISWsb6GhLppbeI3LKpA/content"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Address the controller on the BACnet MS/TP trunk (manually or with auto addressing), then release the box to application control. The BMS commands occupancy with OCC.UNOCC (BO 29), sets heat/cool mode with HEAT.COOL (BO 5) for the season, writes the occupied setpoints, and reads room temperature, airflow, reheat valve position and the error status.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 29",
        "name": "OCC.UNOCC",
        "why": "OCC = occupied, UNOCC = unoccupied"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 5",
        "name": "HEAT.COOL",
        "why": "Seasonal HEAT/COOL; no automatic switchover"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 6",
        "name": "OCC CLG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 7",
        "name": "OCC HTG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "ROOM TEMP",
        "why": "Space temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 35",
        "name": "AIR VOLUME",
        "why": "Measured box airflow, cfm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 53",
        "name": "VLV POS",
        "why": "Reheat valve position, %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 99",
        "name": "ERROR STATUS",
        "why": "Controller error code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Occupancy is OCC.UNOCC (BO 29). With a wall switch on DI 2 and WALL SWITCH (BO 18) = YES, the switch sets it; standalone with no switch the controller stays occupied; on a network the field panel or BMS commands OCC.UNOCC. UNOCC OVRD (BO 21) shows a temporary occupied override from the room unit button.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": "PPCL or the field panel must command HEAT.COOL (BO 5) for seasonal switchover; the reheat valve modulates to hold room temperature in either mode.",
    "setup": [
      "BACnet MS/TP only. CTLR ADDRESS (AO 1) holds the MS/TP address; the factory value is 255.",
      "APPLICATION (AO 2) holds the application number; the point table lists its factory default as 6694."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "As shipped, the controller keeps all equipment OFF until it is released to application control (see Siemens start-up procedures).",
      "With a digital room unit (revision 26 and later), a command sent through the room unit puts the matching BACnet input Out Of Service.",
      "Loop gains, motor timing, rotation angles and setup codes are commissioning values; don't write them from the BMS routinely.",
      "UNOCC FLOW (AO 31) may be set equal to or below OCC FLOW (AO 32), never above it."
    ]
  },
